1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,148
If your partner keeps elbowing you awake over your snoring, before you blame your age, check what you ate before bed.

2
00:00:06,516 --> 00:00:13,098
Snoring happens when your airway narrows during sleep and the soft tissue around it vibrates as air squeezes through.

3
00:00:13,466 --> 00:00:18,163
Three foods common on the American dinner table can each narrow that airway differently.

4
00:00:18,531 --> 00:00:21,538
First, processed meats like bacon and deli cold cuts.

5
00:00:21,906 --> 00:00:27,553
They're loaded with sodium and nitrates, which may contribute to fluid retention and swelling in throat tissue.

6
00:00:27,921 --> 00:00:30,322
Second, soda and other sugary drinks.

7
00:00:30,690 --> 00:00:37,735
Drinking them regularly can drive weight gain over time, and extra fat around the neck thickens the airway wall from the outside.

8
00:00:38,103 --> 00:00:40,728
Third, spicy, greasy takeout like hot wings.

9
00:00:41,096 --> 00:00:47,864
That combo can trigger acid reflux, and stomach acid creeping into the throat may irritate airway tissue right as you lie down.

10
00:00:48,232 --> 00:00:58,431
Try freshly cooked chicken or turkey breast instead of bacon and deli meat, sparkling water instead of soda, and finish spicy or fried meals at least three hours before bedtime.

11
00:00:58,799 --> 00:01:01,873
Sleeping on your side instead of your back helps too.
